From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: label asynchronous NaSta payload as a response

The GetNaSta RBUS method accepts an UnassocStaQuery document and later
publishes a different document on Device.WiFi.EM.NaStaResponse.  The encoder
left SubDocName set to UnassocStaQuery, making the response indistinguishable
from a reflected request and causing the EasyMesh agent to reject it.

Name the published document after its actual response object.  This changes
only the internal OneWifi webconfig envelope; the RBUS method/event names and
the EasyMesh 1905 wire representation remain unchanged.

This encoder is shipped by ccsp-one-wifi-libwebconfig; patching only the
ccsp-one-wifi source copy does not alter the runtime shared library.

diff --git a/source/webconfig/wifi_webconfig_nasta.c b/source/webconfig/wifi_webconfig_nasta.c
--- a/source/webconfig/wifi_webconfig_nasta.c
+++ b/source/webconfig/wifi_webconfig_nasta.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
  * Response JSON (produced by encode_nasta_query_subdoc):
  * {
  *   "Version": "1.0",
- *   "SubDocName": "UnassocStaQuery",
+ *   "SubDocName": "UnassociatedSTALinkMetricsResponse",
  *   "UnassociatedSTALinkMetricsResponse": {
  *     "num_sta": 2,
  *     "sta_list": [
@@ -102,7 +102,8 @@ webconfig_error_t encode_nasta_query_subdoc(webconfig_t *config,
     }
 
     cJSON_AddStringToObject(json, "Version", "1.0");
-    cJSON_AddStringToObject(json, "SubDocName", "UnassocStaQuery");
+    cJSON_AddStringToObject(json, "SubDocName",
+        "UnassociatedSTALinkMetricsResponse");
 
     resp_obj = cJSON_CreateObject();
     if (resp_obj == NULL) {
